title Experiment 6 - map: does false sharing hurt atomics too?
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

* Exp 6: false sharing, plain vs atomic
** Question
*** Project 05 predicted atomics would suffer far more from false sharing
*** Does the penalty grow when the increment is a locked RMW?
** Setup
*** Two threads on CPU 2 and CPU 4, 10 M increments each
*** Five configurations, order rotating in one run
**** plain packed and plain padded
**** fetch_add packed and fetch_add padded
**** fetch_add shared (both threads on one counter)
** Results, slowest-thread ns per increment
*** plain packed 1.02, plain padded 0.20, ratio 5.1 times
*** fetch_add packed 8.75, fetch_add padded 1.37, ratio 6.4 times
*** fetch_add shared 8.26, so packed is about the same as shared
** Lesson
*** The ratio looks similar, but the absolute penalty is 9 times larger for atomics
*** Two variables in one line cost as much as one shared variable
*** The hardware arbitrates cache lines, not variables
** Concepts to read first
*** Concept 08: packed vs padded layout
*** Concept 07: cache line ping-pong
@endmindmap
